You can define your stop loss as a percentage of your trading balance in Metatrader 5 using the following MQL5 code:

```cpp
// Calculate the stop loss as a percentage of the trading balance
double balance = AccountBalance();
double stopLossPercentage = 0.01; // 1%
double stopLoss = balance * stopLossPercentage;

// Set the stop loss
input double SL = stopLoss;
```

In this code snippet, we first calculate the trading balance using the `AccountBalance()` function. Then, we define the stop loss percentage (1% in this case) and calculate the stop loss value by multiplying the balance by the percentage. Finally, we set the stop loss value using the `input` keyword.

You can customize this code further based on your specific requirements and trading strategy.

